From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:02:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] msm-firmware-loader: mount only the partitions blobs come
 from

Without hexagonrpcd nothing reads dsp or persist's sensor registry, and
the bluetooth blobs are never linked where the kernel looks. Leave the
three unmounted; persist and dsp are journaled ext4, which a read-only
mount still replays into after an unclean Android shutdown.

diff --git a/msm-firmware-loader.sh b/msm-firmware-loader.sh
index 9ecca09..ead95dd 100644
--- a/msm-firmware-loader.sh
+++ b/msm-firmware-loader.sh
@@ -95,12 +95,12 @@ link_path() {
 # Configurations:
 
 # List of partitions to be mounted and inspected for blobs.
+# Only the partitions firmware blobs come from. retroforge runs no hexagonrpcd,
+# so dsp and persist are never read, and persist and dsp are journaled ext4
+# that even a read-only mount replays into after an unclean Android shutdown.
 FW_PARTITIONS="
 	apnhlos
-	bluetooth$(ab_get_slot)
-	dsp$(ab_get_slot)
 	modem$(ab_get_slot)
-	persist
 	vendor$(ab_get_slot)
 	RADIO
 "
